  "actualProductionFlow": [
    "The App owns one observable handoff use case and injects it through AppDependencies. Actual ReaderView construction registers the same Navigator synchronously; the use case verifies the actual shared position owner identity.",
    "App submission awaits actual Navigator three-field positions, existing BookStore shelf/reading writer and existing BookSourceStore streamed writer before Upgrade. Sealed receipts originate only in their real IO cores; a queue barrier, supplied hash or arbitrary success callback cannot create them.",
    "The actual authenticated install before-first-Upgrade-byte hook awaits the handoff, rechecks the vault lease and commits the exact selected file facts/active positions in the same fsync/rename Upgrade-intent journal record.",
    "Actual BookStore ordinary and strict saves now stop on real chapter-write errors. Legacy inline-TOC migration reuses the same protected reading-union -> shelf -> reading-prune core and only deletes unchanged legacy input after both metadata files and chapters succeeded.",
    "Current-process material comparison reads Bundle.main through the full existing verifier, compares authenticated CodeDirectories/certificates/profiles/identities and accepts no caller-supplied installed directory as current process proof.",
    "Normal-data observation uses original normal-loader book/source receipts plus bounded checked position reads. A true startup bootstrap is distinguished; matching selected bytes in a reopened owner within the same process keeps different-process false.",
    "Unknown Upgrade phases remain Lookup-only. Matching files never authorize deletion, resubmission, Apple authority, kernel-loaded image or automatic renewal."
  ],
